WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.988
And the calendar isn't
the agency's any more.

2
00:00:02.988 --> 00:00:05.837
Policy and vendors set
the dates from outside.

3
00:00:05.837 --> 00:00:10.749
Some have already passed:
M-22-09's Zero Trust actions were

4
00:00:10.749 --> 00:00:14.475
due by the end of fiscal 2024,
and they're still in force.

5
00:00:14.475 --> 00:00:15.725
Others are close.

6
00:00:15.725 --> 00:00:20.573
FedRAMP's Consolidated Rules become
mandatory on January 1, 2027,

7
00:00:20.573 --> 00:00:26.678
except that two of them, vulnerability
detection and response and vulnerability

8
00:00:26.678 --> 00:00:31.975
evaluation and reporting, became
mandatory earlier, on December 7, 2026.

9
00:00:31.975 --> 00:00:39.787
BOD 26-02 wants listed end-of-support
edge devices gone by February 5, 2027.

10
00:00:39.787 --> 00:00:44.992
And by the program's own count,
not a date OMB published,

11
00:00:44.992 --> 00:00:50.788
the Agency Logging Plan under
M-26-14 is due November 18, 2026.

12
00:00:50.788 --> 00:00:56.645
Vendors add their own clock: Windows
Server 2016 ends support on January 12,

13
00:00:56.645 --> 00:01:01.651
2027, and this workbook plans on
those servers being gone by then.

14
00:01:01.651 --> 00:01:03.325
The slide lists the rest.

15
00:01:03.325 --> 00:01:05.162
Nothing fails on a single date.

16
00:01:05.162 --> 00:01:09.520
But every one of these deadlines
assumes the agency knows what it runs,

17
00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:11.450
who owns it, and what governs it.
